course: dictionary
lesson: 15768
title: Tubular: shaped like a tube
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you what a thing looks like or what it is made of. When you meet a new word, look at the words around it for clues. «The bird's beak was long and tubular, like a drinking straw.» The words long and like a drinking straw are the clues, so tubular means shaped like a tube.
explain: A tube is long, round and hollow inside, like a pipe. «The bike frame was made of tubular steel, so it was light but strong.» Here tubular tells you what the frame is made of: hollow metal tubes. Try your meaning in the sentence: "made of hollow metal tubes" still makes sense.
explain: Tubular can also describe a kind of musical instrument. «The band played tubular bells at the end of the concert.» Tubular bells are long metal tubes that you hit, so the word names the instrument, not a sound.
explain: Some older words change their meaning. Long ago, in surfer talk in the USA, tubular meant great or cool. You will rarely hear it that way now, so in school it usually means shaped like a tube or made of tubes.
fact: Tubular means shaped like a tube: long, round and hollow, like a pipe or a drinking straw.
fact: Tubular also means made of tubes, as in «a tubular steel chair frame».
fact: Hollow tubes are strong but light, which is why engineers use tubular steel in bikes and bridges.
fact: «Tubular bells» are long metal tubes that you hit to make a sound.
fact: Old-fashioned US slang: «tubular» once meant great or cool, but this use is rare today.
exercise: «The bird's beak was long and tubular, like a drinking straw.» What does tubular describe? | Its colour, bright and blue | *Its shape, long and hollow like a tube | Its sound, loud and sharp | Its smell, sweet and strong
exercise: Mia's bike frame is made of tubular steel. What is the frame made of? | *Hollow metal tubes | Soft cloth | Wet paper | Plastic bricks
exercise: «The band played tubular bells at the end of the concert.» What are tubular bells? | Bells made of soft wool | Flat bells that you tap with a stick | *Long metal tubes that you hit | Round bells that you shake
test: Which thing is most like a tubular shape? | *A drinking straw | A cube | A ball | A coin
test: Tubular bells are a kind of what? | Piece of furniture | Type of bird | *Musical instrument | Vegetable
exam: «The tubular frame made the chair light but strong.» What does this tell you about tubular? | *It is shaped like a tube, made of hollow pipes | It is a soft, woolly material | It is a kind of food | It is a loud, sharp sound
